1. All goods owned by foreign organizations or individuals may be transited through the Vietnamese territory and only need to go through customs procedures at the border gates of importation and exportation as prescribed by law, except for the following cases:
a. Weapons, ammunition, explosives and other highly dangerous goods, unless otherwise permitted by the Prime Minister;

Article 240. - Obligations of logistics service providers when holding goods. When not yet exercising the right to dispose of goods under Article 239 of this Law, a logistics service provider exercising the right to hold goods has the following obligations:
1. - Storage and preservation of goods;
2. The goods must not be used without the consent of the party having the seized goods;
3. Returning goods when the conditions for holding or disposing of goods specified in Article 239 of this Law no longer exist;
Fourth. To pay damages to the party having the seized goods if they are lost or damaged.
